e and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/9003cc9588b0838527f018463e2077d2d81bb5930ab70c1e3c713832e207bd99.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58b04cc-da5e-5c51-a583-0663d783c697" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Slope Fields Corresponding to Some Equilibrium Point Classifications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82f05d1c-61d9-5838-994e-c7feddc4294b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-96557-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147020} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7562c8-0d8c-5377-b4fa-8f1a84574df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-96557-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147021} {:answer/id #uuid "d3507101-2ea6-55cd-b72b-689dff9a483c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-96557-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147022} {:answer/id #uuid "e430f9b3-8406-5868-9839-7c38b88b3ca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Image