that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/074ed04c41f20a891678d61a26ae06f1151299110dfd13d2c8b7f6eef3e6e363.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solution:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a node because it is neither a source nor a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-3$ is a node\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58b04cc-da5e-5c51-a583-0663d783c697" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Slope Fields Corresponding to Some Equilibrium Point Classifications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18f47973-dc40-5a25-bfe7-4ec27d53d565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/a375a537b104f5bcdd8f5951277bce2494d8861a7212772a7d7050fa14091cb9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318242} {:answer/id #uuid "6c326e90-6df7-57bc-a33b-babe0a3f367c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/c7895d3f3db254736c4e20ff30dbe92fb7c0786291b1198ed3f727971268be31.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318243} {:answer/id #uuid "1ccc9153-04b8-5c60-8a77-dbb5e48ff9b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/d72110682c1959f10546b6fa49d6e4ebedf6b6d5557639c772f28a920f306df5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318244} {:answer/id #uuid "4b513102-c6f7-578d-ad85-e594a933be90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/41f32a097325dbe2a278da2abe4ef93b13d058ffe49431882fade3bc40bc0f48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318245} {:answer/id #uuid "22ddb781-c3a2-5f6e-a938-f69e1376906c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/31519aa878fd6a9b450296552afd9bbf628e30db68a2d7c6dc6b02a48ae28b06.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b513102-c6f7-578d-ad85-e594a933be90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/41f32a097325dbe2a278da2abe4ef93b13d058ffe49431882fade3bc40bc0f48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318245} :answer-field/id #uuid "911d25e4-075e-5940-968d-92f845da40f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df1a08a1-49b6-5687-bf86-dc8094436b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-98774" :question/problem "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=0$ is a source\n\n- $y=-4$ is a sink\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $2$ equilibrium points, $y=0$ and $y=-4.$\n\n- We're given that $y=0$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=0$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-4$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-4$ (already drawn by the above property) and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/e5ba765b9caffab904f07c5086d3206f72e36e66cb018673ce7ed44d79d19e88.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/41f32a097325dbe2a278da2abe4ef93b13d058ffe49431882fade3bc40bc0f48.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=0$ and $y=-4.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=0$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=-4$ appear to converge toward this line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58b04cc-da5e-5c51-a583-0663d783c697" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Slope Fields Corresponding to Some Equilibrium Point Classifications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "997399f0-925a-5c8f-ace4-5d78470b3e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147074} {:answer/id #uuid "b5acf733-265f-5438-b980-a858541be544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147075} {:answer/id #uuid "1d9a7822-23ae-5632-8a20-2b547498ec0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147076} {:answer/id #uuid "258ed779-50f1-521d-9dc8-17d86ffa3684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147077} {:answer/id #uuid "61cc2e38-a7db-5d9e-9599-3bfb95c8a016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "258ed779-50f1-521d-9dc8-17d86ffa3684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2533/Source/Images/q-98811-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147077} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a4807be-6348-5710-b770-10e19a33d53c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186147073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b626551c-31fe-589e-860a-053b0e741b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-98811" :question/problem "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-2$ is a source\n\n- $y=0$ is a sink\n\n- $y=2$ is a source\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-2,$ $y=0,$ and $y=2.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-2$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-2$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=0$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=0$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n- We're given that $y=2$ is also a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=2$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it (already drawn by the above property).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/b5afe944331145c5253b2f1100f642b8a91a538295f3c84877eeb86870a04915.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/fb27ad885fc87fa56a04ec92d46173c98fda170f11117c4748c21a67faa9e166.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2,$ $y=0,$ and $y=2.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=0$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=2$ appear to diverge away from this line."}]}
